#. module: powerbi_portal
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:powerbi_portal.field_ad_group_sync_config__use_odoo_ldap
msgid ""
"Read the AD server/port/TLS/base/bind settings from Odoo's own LDAP "
"Authentication config (Settings > Technical > LDAP Configuration, "
"res.company.ldap - the same connection used for LDAP login) instead of "
"entering them here. Enable so the AD connection always matches what Odoo "
"uses for login - change it once there, not here."
msgstr ""

#. module: powerbi_portal
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:powerbi_portal.field_pbirs_discovery_config__auth_mode
msgid ""
"Recommended: 'Windows Trusted Connection (Kerberos)' if the Odoo service "
"runs as your dedicated AD service account with a valid Kerberos TGT - reuses"
" that identity automatically via pyodbc's Kerberos support (works on both "
"Windows and Linux), no SQL credentials stored in Odoo. On Windows, this uses"
" SSPI; on Linux it uses GSSAPI - requires the machine to be domain-joined or"
" have a valid keytab/kinit for the service account. Grant that account just "
"db_datareader on this database - avoid using 'sa' or any sysadmin login "
"here, this connection is read-only anyway."
msgstr ""

#. module: powerbi_portal
#: model:ir.model.fields,field_description:powerbi_portal.field_powerbi_report__url
msgid "Report URL"
msgstr ""

#. module: powerbi_portal
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:powerbi_portal.field_pbirs_discovery_config__use_api
msgid ""
"Route PBIRS discovery AND access push through the Windows Access Management "
"API (FastAPI on the BI host), instead of reading the PBIRS SQL database "
"directly and pushing via SOAP. The API runs on the BI host with the correct "
"Windows/AD service identity, so Odoo needs no Kerberos/SSPI/NTLM libs or an "
"ODBC driver for PBIRS access - and it also unlocks SSAS/AD/local group "
"provisioning from the same endpoint. Enable once the FastAPI Base URL and "
"API Key below are set."
msgstr ""

